{"id": "EUVD-2026-103044", "enisaUuid": "37871499-9955-3fde-8d25-3e0cf22f0e54", "description": "smart-sso through 2.1.1 contains an open redirect vulnerability in the /login handler that allows unauthenticated attackers to steal OAuth2 authorization codes by supplying an unvalidated redirectUri parameter. Attackers can send crafted /login links to users with active SSO sessions, then redeem stolen codes at /oauth2/access_token with any valid client credentials to obtain victims' access tokens.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:38:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:29:48", "baseScore": 7.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/smart-sso-oauth2-code-leak-open-redirect", "https://github.com/a466350665/smart-sso/blob/2.1.1/smart-sso-server/src/main/java/com/smart/sso/server/controller/LoginController.java#L53-L63", "https://github.com/a466350665/smart-sso/blob/1.6.0/smart-sso-server/src/main/java/openjoe/smart/sso/server/controller/LoginController.java#L50-L59", "https://github.com/a466350665/smart-sso/blob/1.6.0/smart-sso-server/src/main/java/openjoe/smart/sso/server/controller/Oauth2Controller.java#L55-L84", "https://github.com/a466350665/smart-sso", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/smart-sso-through-2.1.1-oauth2-authorization-code-theft-via-unvalidated-redirecturi"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7rfc-8j8f-xgwj", "CVE-2026-111622"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.43, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "cccb3665-56c0-3a35-9866-ba1f36ebca56", "product": {"name": "Smart-SSO", "vendor": {"name": "a466350665"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.1.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "187d8c77-6751-3f16-8df9-8c8cec11c4dd", "vendor": {"name": "a466350665"}}], "isExploited": false}